 "memo": "Grouped each cell by the action or concern a policy names, after reading the whole cell, and reused one label for the same idea across cells (e.g. 'Citing and disclosing AI use', 'Keeping data out of AI tools', 'Using approved AI tools', 'Verifying AI output', 'AI as a study aid', 'Asking when unsure', 'Effects of AI on learning', 'Flaws in AI output'). Groups are ordered by summed university counts. Hard calls: uploading course materials and recording lectures went under 'Keeping data out of AI tools'; in instructor course-start, instructors telling students how to cite AI and instructors disclosing their own AI use share 'Citing and disclosing AI use'; in the large instructor before-course cell, assessment-design items were kept as one big redesign group rather than split by tactic, to stay within seven groups; single-policy groups were kept only where the policy is clearly distinct (e.g. P92.06 approved tools, P97.13 assistive technology, P55.01 tracking learning impact); the all-inst background cell needed a broad 'Variation in AI rules' group for policy-scope facts (no single policy, rules differ by course, AI framed as a helper)."
}